# .atlas.conf — the only per-repo Atlas configuration.
# Sourced by scripts/atlas-*.sh, which are otherwise byte-identical in every
# component repo so they can be checksum-verified against the method templates.
SLUG="<slug>"
ATLAS_VAULT_REMOTE="https://github.com/<org>/Atlas-<Project>.git"

# Optional overrides — defaults shown.
# ATLAS_VAULT=.atlas
# ATLAS_METHOD=.atlas-method
# ATLAS_METHOD_REMOTE=https://github.com/OneMoreRabbit/Atlas.git
#
# Desk layout: ATLAS_VAULT may point at an existing checkout instead of a clone.
# On Windows, spell it the way your tools report paths (e.g. G:/Projects/Atlas-X,
# forward slashes) so the write guard's path match agrees with hook payloads.
# Sharing one checkout is fine for READING only: each publishing component needs
# its own clone — the atlas/<slug>/<topic> branch is per-checkout state (§9).

# Cross-vault needs (1.27.2, optional): the estate's needs register, read in place with
# the vault-read token. Unset = single-vault project, atlas-needs.py stays inert.
# ATLAS_NEEDS_REGISTER="https://api.github.com/repos/<org>/Atlas-Orchestrator/contents/registries/needs.json?ref=dev"
# Cross-vault consumers (1.28, optional): the estate's edges register — every vault's
# external: entries — so a provider can see which other vaults pin its contracts.
# Unset = atlas-needs.py writes no consumers.md.
# ATLAS_EDGES_REGISTER="https://api.github.com/repos/<org>/Atlas-Orchestrator/contents/registries/edges.json?ref=dev"

